          <!-- Introduction -->
          <p>As a web developer, each project offers new challenges and opportunities to grow. My most recent project, a
            website for Bubbles & Fur, was no exception. This was my first time creating a site for someone else, and
            I’m proud of the progress I’ve made. I wanted to take a moment to reflect on what went well and where I see
            room for improvement.</p>
          <p><em>*Note: This version has undergone several updates and is no longer live. You can see the original
              archived on <a href="https://github.com/bgweaver/bubblesandfur_old" target="_blank">GitHub</a>. You can
              also see the latest version live at <a href="https://www.bubblesandfur.com" target="_blank">Bubbles &
                Fur</a> or on <a href="https://github.com/bgweaver/bubblesandfur" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.</em></p>

          <!-- What I'm Proud Of -->
          <h4 class="section-heading"><strong>What I’m Proud Of:</strong></h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>First Published Site for a Client:</strong> This was my first official project for someone else,
              and seeing it live was incredibly rewarding. Delivering a site that meets a client’s needs feels like a
              milestone.</li>
            <li><strong>Used Netlify for Deployment:</strong> This was my first time using Netlify, which made the
              deployment process smooth and efficient.</li>
            <li><strong>Form Integration:</strong> I implemented Netlify Forms with honeypot and CAPTCHA features to
              reduce spam, a critical improvement from past experiences.</li>
            <li><strong>Custom Email Setup:</strong> Using ImprovMX, I set up a custom email address, enhancing the
              client’s brand credibility.</li>
            <li><strong>Animation with AOS:</strong> Subtle animations added a dynamic element, making the first
              impression more engaging.</li>
            <li><strong>Meeting the Client Brief:</strong> I adapted quickly to client requests, ensuring the final
              product aligned with her vision.</li>
            <li><strong>About Page Creation:</strong> I crafted an “About the Business” page using the client’s
              interview responses, adding a personal touch.</li>
            <li><strong>Expanded Use of Bootstrap:</strong> I made the layout responsive and got the navigation bar behaving properly.</li>
            <li><strong>Meta Tags for Enhanced Sharing:</strong> Implementing meta tags improved how the site appears on
              social media and messaging apps.</li>
            <li><strong>Site Indexing and Google Business Entry:</strong> Indexing the site improved its visibility and
              online presence.</li>
          </ul>

          <!-- Wishes and Next Steps -->
          <h4 class="section-heading"><strong>Wishes and Next Steps:</strong></h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Integrating Payment:</strong> The next step is adding a payment system like Clover or PayPal,
              which will be a learning opportunity.</li>
            <li><strong>Improving Bootstrap Skills:</strong> I want to enhance my layouts and solve centering issues
              more effectively.</li>
            <li><strong>Enhancing Visual Appeal:</strong> Some pages lack visual interest, so I’ll focus on improving
              design principles.</li>
            <li><strong>Expanding My Client Base:</strong> My goal is to publish a site for a non-relative client,
              expanding my portfolio.</li>
            <li><strong>Creating a Portfolio Site:</strong> I aim to build a custom site showcasing my work and skills.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <!-- Conclusion -->
          <p>This project was a real step forward for me. I’m happy with the progress and motivated by the challenges ahead. Each project is a learning experience, and I can’t wait to
            see where the next one takes me.</p>
